{
  "dom_id": "step-q184770",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Let $n$ be an integer. Prove that ${n}^{3}$ is even implies $n$ is even.\n\nThe contrapositive form of the given statement is as follows:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\\,⇒\\,{{field-2}}\n$$\n\nWe will prove this statement instead of the original one.\n\nIf $n$ is {{field-3}}, then $n=$ {{field-4}} for some integer $a.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{3} & ={{field-5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
